# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Formal equivalence filter for one MCY mutation.
#
# Reads the unmutated MCY database netlist as `gold` and the mutant produced
# by create_mutated.sh as `gate`, builds an $equiv miter over matching named
# wires, and attempts an unbounded proof:
#
#   equiv_simple  local (combinational / short sequential) equivalence points
#   equiv_induct  temporal induction over the remaining points
#
# `equiv_status -assert` makes yosys exit non-zero unless every equivalence
# point is proven. The proof direction is one-sided on purpose: success means
# the mutant is provably indistinguishable at the module boundary for all
# input sequences and all states, so it is a NOCHANGE (equivalent) mutant.
# Failure means "not proven equivalent" - which includes both genuinely
# non-equivalent mutants and mutants whose equivalence needs a reachability
# invariant that plain temporal induction cannot supply. Unproven therefore
# stays inside the coverage denominator, which is the conservative direction
# for an evidence-gated project.
#
# -seq 30 covers the 24-iteration multiply plus handshake slack.

read_rtlil ../../database/design.il
rename lca_butterfly gold

read_rtlil mutated.il
rename lca_butterfly gate

equiv_make gold gate equiv
hierarchy -top equiv
opt_clean

equiv_simple -seq 30
equiv_induct -seq 30
equiv_status -assert
